From: custom
Subject: [PATCH] mt7981 cudy tr3000 256mb: multi mtd layout + switchable vendor bootargs

Upstream already ships the machinery for "one U-Boot, several partition maps":
a board DTS lists them under /mtd-layout, board_mtdparts_default() picks one by
the `mtd_layout_label` environment variable, and the web failsafe can switch it
from the upgrade page. The 128 MiB Cudy TR3000 has that support
(configs/mt7981_cudy_tr3000-v1_multi_layout_defconfig); the 256 MiB variant
does not, and its DTS has no /mtd-layout node at all.

Add it, and while at it stop hard-coding the vendor command line:

  * configs/mt7981_cudy_tr3000-v1-256mb_multi_layout_defconfig (new)
    Same as the plain 256 MiB defconfig, minus MTDIDS_DEFAULT/MTDPARTS_DEFAULT
    (the layouts provide them now), plus MEDIATEK_MULTI_MTD_LAYOUT and
    CMD_SHOW_MTD_LAYOUT.

  * arch/arm/dts/mt7981-cudy-tr3000-v1-256mb.dts
    /mtd-layout with
      layout@0 "default" -- the Cudy factory map, plus the command line the
                            stock images do not carry themselves
      layout@1 "112m"    -- 112 MiB UBI for the ubootmod / 112m-nmbm images
    The first five partitions are identical in both maps, so BL2 and the FIP
    never move and only the UBI size changes.

  * board/mediatek/common/mtd_helper.c
    mtd_vendor_bootargs_setup() used to clear "bootargs" and inject
    ubi.rootfs_volume=rootfs plus a set of boot_param.* entries. That makes the
    kernel look for its root filesystem the UBIFS way while the volume actually
    holds squashfs, which ends in an endless reboot loop. The command line now
    comes from the active layout (which is also what the stock layouts upstream
    do -- their default layout sets the console settings and nothing else), and
    the new `vendor_bootargs` variable can replace it verbatim, so trying
    another parameter set costs one setenv + mtkboardboot instead of a rebuild.

Requires 0001, 0002 and 0003.

Apply with:
    git apply 0004-uboot-multi-layout-cudy-256mb.patch
Fallback if your tree normalises EOLs differently:
    git apply --ignore-whitespace 0004-uboot-multi-layout-cudy-256mb.patch
    patch -p1 -l < 0004-uboot-multi-layout-cudy-256mb.patch

---
diff --git a/uboot-mtk-20250711/arch/arm/dts/mt7981-cudy-tr3000-v1-256mb.dts b/uboot-mtk-20250711/arch/arm/dts/mt7981-cudy-tr3000-v1-256mb.dts
index 6e690b4..95c4752 100644
--- a/uboot-mtk-20250711/arch/arm/dts/mt7981-cudy-tr3000-v1-256mb.dts
+++ b/uboot-mtk-20250711/arch/arm/dts/mt7981-cudy-tr3000-v1-256mb.dts
@@ -22,6 +22,50 @@
 		system_led = "red:power";
 	};
 
+	/*
+	 * Two partition maps for one board, selected at run time through the
+	 * `mtd_layout_label` environment variable (web UI: 高级功能 -> MTD 布局).
+	 *
+	 * The first five partitions are identical in both, so BL2 and the FIP
+	 * never move: only the size of the UBI partition changes. Nothing in
+	 * the boot chain outside U-Boot has to know which map is active.
+	 */
+	mtd-layout {
+		/*
+		 * layout@0 -- Cudy factory layout.
+		 *
+		 * Byte for byte the map the stock bootloader hands to the stock
+		 * firmware, so an image written by this U-Boot boots with exactly
+		 * the partitioning it was built for, and UBI keeps the size it
+		 * already has on the flash.
+		 *
+		 * The stock images carry only their console settings in
+		 * /chosen/bootargs -- everything else used to live in the factory
+		 * environment, which does not survive another firmware writing the
+		 * env partition. Supply it here instead. `ubi.mtd` is what makes
+		 * the kernel attach the UBI device; the rootfs volume itself is
+		 * resolved by the kernel's own default rootdev logic, so there is
+		 * deliberately no `root=`.
+		 */
+		layout@0 {
+			label = "default";
+			mtdids = "nmbm0=nmbm0";
+			mtdparts = "nmbm0:1024k(bl2),512k(u-boot-env),2048k(Factory),256k(bdinfo),2048k(fip),-(ubi)";
+			cmdline = "console=ttyS0,115200n1 loglevel=8 ubi.mtd=ubi";
+		};
+
+		/*
+		 * layout@1 -- 112 MiB UBI, the layout the ubootmod / 112m-nmbm
+		 * images for this board expect. Those bring a complete command
+		 * line of their own, so none is set here.
+		 */
+		layout@1 {
+			label = "112m";
+			mtdids = "nmbm0=nmbm0";
+			mtdparts = "nmbm0:1024k(bl2),512k(u-boot-env),2048k(Factory),256k(bdinfo),2048k(fip),114688k(ubi)";
+		};
+	};
+
 	memory@40000000 {
 		device_type = "memory";
 		reg = <0x40000000 0x20000000>;
diff --git a/uboot-mtk-20250711/board/mediatek/common/mtd_helper.c b/uboot-mtk-20250711/board/mediatek/common/mtd_helper.c
index d48f197..282747d 100644
--- a/uboot-mtk-20250711/board/mediatek/common/mtd_helper.c
+++ b/uboot-mtk-20250711/board/mediatek/common/mtd_helper.c
@@ -1411,47 +1411,49 @@ static int ubi_dual_boot(struct mtd_info *mtd, bool do_boot)
 }
 
 /*
- * Vendor images (the stock MTK-SDK / OpenWrt firmware) keep the kernel FIT in
- * the UBI volume named "kernel" and the squashfs root filesystem in the
- * volume named "rootfs". Their embedded /chosen/bootargs carries only the
- * console settings -- the kernel has to be *told* which UBI volume is the
- * root filesystem, through the MTK parameters below.
+ * Vendor images (the stock MTK-SDK / Cudy firmware) keep the kernel FIT in the
+ * UBI volume named "kernel" and the squashfs root filesystem in the volume
+ * named "rootfs".
  *
- * On the stock bootloader those parameters come from a factory environment
- * that stops existing as soon as anything else writes the env partition, and
- * the kernel then panics with "VFS: Unable to mount root fs" and reboot-loops
- * forever. Rebuild them here.
+ * Their embedded /chosen/bootargs carries the console settings only, and on
+ * the stock bootloader the parameters that tell the kernel where its root
+ * filesystem lives came from a factory environment that stops existing as
+ * soon as anything else writes the env partition. Without a command line the
+ * kernel cannot find its root and reboot-loops forever.
+ *
+ * The command line now comes from the active mtd layout (the `cmdline`
+ * property of /mtd-layout in the board DTS), which board_mtdparts_default()
+ * has already exported through the `bootargs` variable by the time we get
+ * here. Nothing is appended or cleared, so the layout -- or the operator --
+ * remains in charge.
  *
  * Only the "kernel" volume is affected. Images booted from the "fit" volume
  * (our own layout, and OpenWrt's ubootmod) carry a complete command line of
  * their own and are deliberately left alone.
- *
- * The values mirror what MediaTek's own ubi_set_bootargs() puts on the kernel
- * command line for a non-secure-boot build -- note there is no 'root=': the
- * kernel resolves the root filesystem from ubi.rootfs_volume itself.
  */
 static void mtd_vendor_bootargs_setup(void)
 {
+	const char *override;
+
 	if (!ubi_image_vol || strcmp(ubi_image_vol, PART_KERNEL_NAME))
 		return;
 
-	cprintln(PROMPT, "*** Vendor '%s' volume found: supplying MTK UBI bootargs ***",
-		 PART_KERNEL_NAME);
-
 	/*
-	 * A stale command line from a previous firmware would otherwise be
-	 * applied on top of ours by fdt_chosen(), so start from a clean slate.
+	 * `vendor_bootargs` replaces the layout's command line as-is. Trying a
+	 * different parameter set is then a single setenv plus mtkboardboot,
+	 * instead of a firmware rebuild.
 	 */
-	env_set("bootargs", NULL);
-
-	bootargs_set("ubi.mtd", PART_UBI_NAME);
-	bootargs_set("ubi.rootfs_volume", "rootfs");
-	bootargs_set("boot_param.boot_kernel_part", PART_KERNEL_NAME);
-	bootargs_set("boot_param.boot_rootfs_part", "rootfs");
-	bootargs_set("boot_param.upgrade_kernel_part", PART_KERNEL_NAME);
-	bootargs_set("boot_param.upgrade_rootfs_part", "rootfs");
-	bootargs_set("boot_param.env_part", CONFIG_ENV_MTD_DEV);
-	bootargs_set("boot_param.rootfs_data_part", PART_ROOTFS_DATA_NAME);
+	override = env_get("vendor_bootargs");
+	if (override && override[0]) {
+		cprintln(PROMPT, "*** vendor_bootargs override: %s ***", override);
+		env_set("bootargs", override);
+		return;
+	}
+
+	cprintln(PROMPT, "*** Booting vendor '%s' volume with the layout command line ***",
+		 PART_KERNEL_NAME);
+	cprintln(PROMPT, "*** bootargs: %s ***",
+		 env_get("bootargs") ? env_get("bootargs") : "(unset)");
 }
 
 static int boot_from_ubi(struct mtd_info *mtd, bool do_boot)
diff --git a/uboot-mtk-20250711/configs/mt7981_cudy_tr3000-v1-256mb_multi_layout_defconfig b/uboot-mtk-20250711/configs/mt7981_cudy_tr3000-v1-256mb_multi_layout_defconfig
